<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Read-face data refresh, on a schedule (TCRN-AOS-INC-049, Owner ruling of
  2026-08-04: the refresh runs from this machine rather than the VM).

  WHAT PROBLEM THIS SOLVES. The LAN read face serves a BUILD-TIME snapshot. The
  chains move on; the page does not, and nothing about a stale page looks stale —
  it renders perfectly, with last week's answer. That is how a page built on
  2026-08-03 was still being served while a day of governed work sat on the
  chains, invisible to the only surface a human reads without an SSH tunnel.

  WHY THIS MACHINE AND NOT THE VM. Ruled 2026-08-04. Building the data needs the
  web toolchain; the VM has an engine and no node_modules by design, and shipping
  a build toolchain there to serve one page is a larger change than the problem
  warrants. The trade is honest and worth stating: while this laptop is off, the
  read face goes stale, and only the freshness gate says so. That gate is the
  compensating control — `pnpm read-face:freshness` asks the SERVICE what it is
  serving, so nobody has to trust this schedule ran.

  WHY 4 HOURS. Slower than the work arrives, faster than a working day. The data
  build projects five chains serially and takes minutes; running it every few
  minutes would spend the machine on a page nobody is watching at 3am.

  RunAtLoad is false: installing a schedule should not kick off a VM deployment
  at that moment.

  TEMPLATE, NOT A LOADED AGENT — same rule as the paired-backup plist beside it.
  The path is one machine's; loading is the operator's act, not the repository's.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key>
  <string>com.tcrn.aos.read-face-refresh</string>

  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/bin/sh</string>
    <string>-lc</string>
    <string>cd "$HOME/Code/TCRN Platform/TCRN-AOS" &amp;&amp; pnpm cockpit:data &amp;&amp; node deploy/aos-resident-cockpit/apply-read-face.mjs &amp;&amp; pnpm read-face:freshness</string>
  </array>

  <key>StartInterval</key>
  <integer>14400</integer>

  <key>RunAtLoad</key>
  <false/>

  <key>StandardOutPath</key>
  <string>/tmp/tcrn-aos-read-face-refresh.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
  <string>/tmp/tcrn-aos-read-face-refresh.err</string>
</dict>
</plist>
